{"name":"Troll Slayer Orange","hex":"#f4a34c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"troll","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["a giant supernatural being, especially a grotesque humanoid creature living in caves or hills or under bridges. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A type of diminutive supernatural being; a dwarf."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Senses relating to a rolling motion.\n\nTo move (something, especially a round object) by, or as if by, rolling; to bowl, to roll, to trundle. \n\n Often followed by in: to cause (something) to flow or roll in like a stream.\n\nTo roll; also, to turn round and round; to rotate, to spin, to whirl. \n\nTo move or walk at a leisurely pace; to ramble, to saunter, to stroll. \n\n Chiefly of a man: synonym of cruise (“to stroll about to find a (male) sexual partner”). \n Followed by in: to flow or roll in like a stream.","To move (something, especially a round object) by, or as if by, rolling; to bowl, to roll, to trundle. \n\n Often followed by in: to cause (something) to flow or roll in like a stream."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/troll"},{"term":"slayer","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A killer; a murderer; someone who slays.","A butcher."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slayer"},{"term":"orange","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evergreen tree of the genus Citrus such as Citrus sinensis which yields oranges (the fruit).","Any round citrus fruit with a yellow-red colour when ripe and a sour-sweet taste; the fruit of the orange tree.\n Specifically, a sweet orange or Citrus sinensis."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the colour of the fruit of an orange tree; yellowred; reddish-yellow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orange"}],"entries":[{"title":"Troll","blocks":[{"text":"A troll is a being in Nordic folklore, including Norse mythology. In Old Norse sources, beings described as trolls dwell in isolated areas of rocks, mountains, or caves, live together in small family units, and are rarely helpful to human beings."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/John_Bauer_1915.jpg/330px-John_Bauer_1915.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Troll","wikidata":"Q12581"},{"title":"Slayer","blocks":[{"text":"Slayer is an American thrash metal band from Huntington Park, California, formed in 1981 by guitarists Kerry King and Jeff Hanneman, drummer Dave Lombardo and vocalist/bassist Tom Araya. Slayer's fast and aggressive musical style made them one of the \"big four\" bands of thrash metal, alongside Metallica, Megadeth, and Anthrax. Slayer's current lineup comprises King, Araya, drummer Paul Bostaph, and guitarist Gary Holt, who initially joined as a touring musician in 2011 before joining the band permanently after Hanneman's death in 2013; the drummer Jon Dette is a former member of the band."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Slayer%2C_The_Fields_of_Rock%2C_2007.jpg/330px-Slayer%2C_The_Fields_of_Rock%2C_2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slayer","wikidata":"Q131231"},{"title":"Orange (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Orange is the colour between yellow and red on the spectrum of visible light. The human eyes perceive orange when observing light with a dominant wavelength between roughly 585 and 620 nanometres. In traditional colour theory, it is a secondary colour of pigments, produced by mixing yellow and red. In the RGB colour model, it is a tertiary colour. It is named after the fruit of the same name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Delicatearch.png/330px-Delicatearch.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange_(colour)","wikidata":